Transfer Learning Strategy – Key Points
Dataset size and dataset similarity are the two main factors that determine the transfer learning strategy.
If the new dataset is highly similar to the pre-trained dataset, most of the pre-trained model can be reused.
For a small dataset with high similarity, only the final output layer needs to be trained.
If the dataset has low similarity, additional layers must be retrained to learn new features.
For a small dataset with low similarity, freeze the lower layers and fine-tune the higher layers.
If the dataset is large and similar, fine-tuning most or all layers can improve performance.
When the dataset is large and very different from the original dataset, training the model from scratch is usually the best approach.

